# Adapted from eyeling/examples/path-discovery.n3: a real-world air-route
# graph (see https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/database/build-and-deploy-knowledge-graphs-faster-with-rdf-and-opencypher/).
# Keeps the full ~96,000-fact dataset (every airline/airport/city/country
# label and every hasOutboundRouteTo edge) and a fully general, recursive
# `route/6` predicate: it works for any starting airport, any destination,
# and any maximum number of stopovers, exactly like the source N3 rules'
# backward-chained, visited-list-guarded search.
